Abstract = {Decision Support System (DSS) is a support tool in helping users to
   provide suggestions of decisions when the information is disorganized
   and has a complex problem. Eventually, the dynamics of data on certain
   domains is unclear, semantic interoperability and heterogeneous data
   sources. To address solve the problem, the ontology can be applied to
   perform knowledge representation. The aim of this paper is to discuss
   the role of ontology in developing DSS as a supporter of multi-criteria
   decision-making. This study used Kitchenham's methodology to assist in
   literature review. There are five journals electronic databases selected
   as references, such as, Science Direct, IEEE, Google Scholar, JSTOR, and
   Springer Link This study obtained 21 final articles that were
   synthesized to answer research questions. The ontology-based DSS
   delivers a deeper analysis of the decision situation and suggests a new
   methodology which can affords accurate results of calculation. Though
   most of the studies present that the ontology is not integrated with DSS
   techniques.},
