   (MME), Ceske Budejovice, CZECH REPUBLIC, SEP 11-13, 2019},
Organization = {Univ S Bohemia, Fac Econ; Czech Soc Operat Res; Slovak Soc Operat Res;
   Czech Econometr Soc},
Abstract = {The paper proposes the use of semantic networks and analytical network
   analysis (ANP) methods for quantification of the ``soft{''} structure of
   a project in corporate organization. The semantic project networks are
   derived based on the organization structure and on the life cycle of
   projects. Their subsequent quantification using the ANP method creates
   the basis for analysis of the project roles and analysis of their
   individual relationship to organization units. Although the project
   roles during the management of projects are the key to the success, an
   approach to the quantification and analysis of their impact and
   influence on project organization structure has not been introduced yet.
   Semantic networks can be used to manage projects to illustrate and
   quantify links between internal and external objects of the project
   environment - project goals, project outputs, project documents, etc.
   The paper suggests a new approach for identifying and quantifying
   project roles in the project organization management. The showed
   semantic model and its quantification can be used to construct a
   multi-criteria model for decision support in commercial practice. The
   paper contains a case study of application of semantic model of project
   management in commercial organization from bank sector.},
