   Technology-EUSFLAT, Riga, LATVIA, JUL 21-25, 2025},
Organization = {European Society for Fuzzy Logic and Technology; University of Latvia},
Abstract = {In this work, we extend the integration of fuzzy logic in Multi-Criteria
   Group Decision-Making (MCGDM) problems and its application to
   ontologies. We define an MCGDM framework where experts assign scores and
   weights to ontology classes, and each one of them is assigned a fuzzy
   weight, reflecting their relative importance in the decision process.
   Each expert selects their best choice among the alternatives and a final
   best compromise A{*} is derived using a minimal mean distance operator,
   ensuring that the aggregated result optimally reflects expert opinions
   while minimizing deviations from individual preferences.},
