Organization = {IEEE; IEEE Bulgarian Sect; IEEE Poland Sect; IEEE Czechoslovakia Sect
   Comp Soc Chapter; IEEE Poland Sect Syst, Man, \& Cybernet Soc Chapter;
   IEEE Poland Sect, Computat Intelligence Soc Chapter; IEEE Poland Sect,
   Control Syst Soc Chapter; Polish Acad Sci, Comm Comp Sci; Mazovia
   Cluster ICT; Eastern Cluster ICT; SIAM, Bulgarian Sect},
Abstract = {Objective evaluation in problems considering many, often conflicting
   criteria is challenging for the decision-maker. This paper presents an
   approach based on MCDA methods to objectify evaluations in the camera
   selection problem. The proposed approach includes three MCDA methods,
   TOPSIS, VIKOR, COMET, and two criterion weighting techniques. Two
   ranking similarity coefficients were used to compare the resulting
   rankings of the alternatives: WS and r(w). The performed research
   confirmed the importance of the appropriate selection of multi-criteria
   decision-making methods for the solved problem and the relevance of
   comparative analysis in method selection and construction of objective
   rankings of alternatives.},
