Note = {25th KES International Conference on Knowledge-Based and Intelligent
   Information \& Engineering Systems (KES), Szczecin, POLAND, SEP 08-10,
   2021},
Organization = {KES Int},
Abstract = {With the recent rising number of personal drones, the market is growing
   with more and more new drones. The actual number of alternatives is
   unsuspectedly huge. Nevertheless, each year their characteristics are
   only improving, which only complicate the selection. The manual optimal
   choice is a significant challenge, likely even impossible. Still, the
   most efficient way to estimate the ranking of the alternatives is a
   multi-criteria decision analysis (MCDA).
   In this paper, we use MCDA methods towards objective multi-criteria
   drone evaluation. Our work is based on VIKOR and COMET method which have
   presented their efficiency in many works with multi-criteria problems.
   For optimal selection on twelve alternatives of drones, nine criteria
   were used and two MCDA methods with the same weights. Finally, the
   result is presented and discussed in the end. (C) 2021 The Authors.
   Published by Elsevier B.V. This is an open access article under the CC
