Year = {2006},
Pages = {1543+},
Note = {19th IEEE Canadian Conference on Electrical and Computer Engineering,
   Ottawa, CANADA, MAY 07-10, 2006},
Organization = {IEEE},
Abstract = {The present research is devoted to development of a technology of the
   personalized search of learning objects in the Internet, which utilizes
   the learning object's and learner's ontologies, and aggregates the
   software agents for search of educational materials individually for
   each learner. The proposed technology manages the personalized search of
   learning objects for students to support their independent study, for
   employees to continuously improve their professional skills after
   graduation, and for teachers to prepare training material. The present
   paper is focused on the use of learning objects' and learners'
   ontologies developed basing on the OntoClean methodology and IDEF5
   method. The software tool OnToIDEF5 has been created for this purpose.
   These ontologies are devoted to solve the task of personalized search of
   learning objects on the Semantic Web. In order to facilitate this
   search, we propose a semantic mining approach based on multiple
   criteria, which assign learner's preferences using corresponding
   ontologies. For this purpose we introduced criteria of evaluation of
   suitability of educational materials to the learner's profile as well as
   weighting coefficients for each criterion.},
